  "findings": [
    "Five production files implement actual curve extrema, native rounding/minimum dimensions, center rotation and normalized geometry in one point-edit command, including numeric field synchronization. Runtime/renderers and native readers are unchanged.",
    "The actual point-mode TN46 entry writes only changed current-view Location/Size pairs. Shared type/path persist; AutoFit and other view declarations are retained. Affect All Views does not change this entry.",
    "RN4I belongs to separate operations. Early RN4I-based AutoFit/all-view hypotheses and their red tests are retained as superseded evidence, not claimed as ordinary point-edit regressions.",
    "Native AxKeys metadata establishes D1 sharp and D2 round. The previous inverse binding was corrected; broader modifier-dispatch parity remains unverified.",
    "Own point commits retain logical anchor selection; external context/frame changes cancel gestures. Entry/no-op/cancel and numeric editor are independent product transaction policies, not native GUI observations.",
    "Visual inspection found the numeric draft retaining -25 after normalization back to 0. A failing browser assertion established the defect; only point-coordinate fields opt into resetting their draft at commit. The revised build was tested separately.",
    "The tested executable and archived package are verified by hashes; old artifact bytes and reports remain preserved."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Partial-border and independent-corner parameter editing remains gated.",
    "Empty participating segment lists, native general transforms and separate RN4I whole-object commands are not reproduced.",
    "Tiny nonzero rotation dispatch at the retained hN4K 1e-5 threshold is not covered; the current helper uses center rotation for every nonzero angle.",
    "Original UI screenshot capture times out; original pixel/interaction parity is unverified.",
    "Full Axure parity remains incomplete."
  ],
